I(65,'unproved claim',[(34,16,1402,1402),(34,17,1406,1415)],'transport de structure','For a normal open G_{K′}⊂G_K, the action on tame inertia I′_t is cyclotomic through G_k, so I acts trivially on I′_t.','Use the strictly local reduction to pass from normal subgroups of G_K to general open normal subgroups of I.','The replacement argument invokes canonical equivariance; it is a proof sketch with correct scope.')
I(66,'unproved claim',[(34,17,1406,1417)],'extension centrale','For an open normal I′⊂I and P′=ker(I′→I′_t),1→I′_t→I/P′→I/I′→1 is central.','P′ is characteristic in I′, so quotienting is defined; centrality is not splitting.','The note reconstructs the extension explicitly and respects the inserted openness.')
I(67,'idea of the earlier run',[(34,17,1415,1417)],'centrale','For K=C((t)), I≅Zhat(1), I′=mI gives a central extension of Z/m by mI which has no group-homomorphic section because Zhat is torsion-free.','Only splitting as groups is excluded; a set-theoretic continuous section of a finite quotient exists.','The note’s nonsplitting example is correct and is independently checked.')
I(68,'other',[(34,3,1020,1023),(34,5,1101,1107),(34,9,1204,1204),(34,17,1415,1417)],'le th. de monodromie par voie arithmétique','The retained introduction establishes/prepares inertia theory and stops before the quasi-unipotence theorem.','This is a scope conclusion from reading all fifteen leaves, not a theorem’s historical absence.','The note correctly separates promised later applications from the results actually present.')

