I(70,'unpursued implication',[(33,153,179,204),(33,151,129,144)],'Tout a été démontré sauf ... pleinement fidèle','The functor from small Zariski sheaves to big Zariski sheaves is fully faithful, with restriction as a retraction and compatible cohomology.','It is not an equivalence between every big-site and small-site sheaf.','The unit calculation on153 and the Hom argument on151 form a genuine proof continuation.')
I(71,'unproved claim',[(33,149,55,79),(33,147,6,11)],'qui sera démontré dans le § 3','Representable functors satisfying invariance under affine homeomorphisms and filtered affine-limit continuity are claimed to be exactly local isomorphisms over X; their generated minimum topos is Sh(X_Zar).','The exact universal characterization is retained; the completed étalé-space equivalence is distinct from the deferred representable criterion.','The note correctly identifies the missing lemma and the roles of(A),(B).')
I(72,'unpursued implication',[(33,147,11,11)],'aurait la cohomologie nulle en dimension >0','On Spec of a field, every Zariski abelian sheaf has vanishing positive cohomology; stronger topologies detect arithmetic and torsors not Zariski locally trivial.','The historical credit to Serre is this typed author’s narrative, not independently established priority.','The motivation is explicit and the elementary point-space assertion is valid.')
I(73,'unpursued implication',[(33,163,502,506)],'préschéma de Jacobson','For a Jacobson scheme, intersection with the closed-point subspace identifies the lattices of opens and their sheaf topoi.','This does not make the closed-point inclusion a homeomorphism or identify an arbitrary ringed structure.','The modern lattice argument matches the note; the typed formulation also mentions abelian sheaves.')
