I(83,'unpursued implication',[(33,171,698,710)],'Si les G_i sont fermés','In the external locally convex direct sum ⊕E_i, if every G_i⊂E_i is closed, then ⊕G_i is closed, being ⋂p_i^{-1}(G_i). The direct sum represents continuous linear maps coordinatewise.','This makes no claim about arbitrary sums of subspaces inside one fixed space.','The coordinate-projection proof is present and correct.')
I(84,'unproved claim',[(33,175,759,761),(33,173,742,742)],'Follows from [A7, Lemma 3.19 of Section 14]','For regular local(R,m) of dimensionn>1 with parameters x₁,…,x_n, S=R[x₂/x₁,…,x_n/x₁] satisfies S/x₁S≅κ(m)[t₂,…,t_n]; localization at a maximal ideal over x₁ is regular local of dimensionn with finite residue extension.','Maximal centre is essential to the dimension/residue conclusion. The source identity and[A7] remain bibliographical questions.','The lemma is fully stated, but its proof is delegated.')
